WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.128 --> 00:00:01.530
(bass guitar music)

00:00:01.530 --> 00:00:03.300
- [Announcer] From Daytona
International Speedway,

00:00:03.300 --> 00:00:04.490
this is the Motor Racing Network.

00:00:04.490 --> 00:00:06.541
- This sport will break you if you let it.

00:00:06.541 --> 00:00:08.470
(engines roaring)

00:00:08.470 --> 00:00:11.980
I've noticed some faces, like
they're surprised to see me.

00:00:11.980 --> 00:00:13.160
(air drill whirring)

00:00:13.160 --> 00:00:16.801
Historically, NASCAR is Caucasian males.

00:00:16.801 --> 00:00:18.350
(engine revving)

00:00:18.350 --> 00:00:19.370
That's what people think of,

00:00:19.370 --> 00:00:21.270
and that's what they see in the sport.

00:00:22.430 --> 00:00:24.660
Nobody at the track looks like me.

00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:27.493
(uplifting music)

00:00:30.810 --> 00:00:31.980
My name is Brehanna Daniels,

00:00:31.980 --> 00:00:35.060
and I am the first African-American
female pit crew member

00:00:35.060 --> 00:00:36.140
for NASCAR.

00:00:37.130 --> 00:00:39.470
I had no idea that that would happen,

00:00:39.470 --> 00:00:41.550
that's not why I came into this sport,

00:00:41.550 --> 00:00:43.340
but I made history.

00:00:43.340 --> 00:00:45.198
I'm still in shock, to this day.

00:00:45.198 --> 00:00:46.400
(metal tapping)

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:49.170
I was the only girl, but
that actually kind of gave me

00:00:49.170 --> 00:00:50.860
some more motivation, you know,

00:00:50.860 --> 00:00:54.599
to kick the guys' butts I
was goin' against (laughs).

00:00:54.599 --> 00:00:55.799
(brakes squealing)

00:00:55.799 --> 00:00:59.430
I have to work twice as
hard as the next man does.

00:00:59.430 --> 00:01:01.370
It's like I already have like
two targets on my back:

00:01:01.370 --> 00:01:04.080
I’m a female, I’m African-American.

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:05.730
But everything I get, I work for.

00:01:07.061 --> 00:01:08.750
(blues music)

00:01:08.750 --> 00:01:12.761
Pit stops usually range
between, like, 10 and 14 seconds.

00:01:12.761 --> 00:01:13.770
(air drill whirring)

00:01:13.770 --> 00:01:14.900
Everybody has to move quick.

00:01:14.900 --> 00:01:16.440
(blues music)

00:01:16.440 --> 00:01:18.060
There's a front tire changer,

00:01:18.060 --> 00:01:19.520
a front tire carrier,

00:01:19.520 --> 00:01:20.690
a rear tire carrier,

00:01:20.690 --> 00:01:22.790
a gas man and a jack man.

00:01:22.790 --> 00:01:24.441
And I am a rear tire changer.

00:01:24.441 --> 00:01:27.090
(blues music)

00:01:27.090 --> 00:01:30.460
We train year round 'cause you
have to have that strength.

00:01:30.460 --> 00:01:31.920
This isn't just about car mechanics,

00:01:31.920 --> 00:01:32.841
you have to be an athlete.

00:01:32.841 --> 00:01:34.530
(blues music)

00:01:34.530 --> 00:01:35.760
You know, we're really in charge

00:01:35.760 --> 00:01:36.750
of hookin' that driver up

00:01:36.750 --> 00:01:38.400
and makin' sure he's good to go.

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:40.370
Our pit stop has to be on point,

00:01:40.370 --> 00:01:43.200
everybody has to come
together and work as one team

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:46.119
to send our driver off,
to have him in good hands.

00:01:46.119 --> 00:01:47.220
(blues music)

00:01:47.220 --> 00:01:49.409
- [Man] Good job.

00:01:49.409 --> 00:01:51.490
(quiet uplifting music)

00:01:51.490 --> 00:01:54.260
- My mission is to make
sure to be that face

00:01:54.260 --> 00:01:57.470
for women of color and
little boys and little girls,

00:01:59.380 --> 00:02:01.150
and I hope that, one day,

00:02:01.150 --> 00:02:02.860
you know, when people
will think of NASCAR,

00:02:02.860 --> 00:02:05.470
they see it as multiple
faces and not just one.

00:02:06.870 --> 00:02:08.260
I want everybody to join this sport.

00:02:08.260 --> 00:02:09.093
Come on (laughs)!

00:02:10.904 --> 00:02:12.962
(engines roaring)

00:02:12.962 --> 00:02:16.295
(quiet uplifting music)

